{{apichanges|11.2.0|prev=11.1.7|next=11.2.5}}

==Summary==
* Added support for user-configurable font scaling to some parts of the UI, such as dialogs.
* Added support for the <span class="apitype">[TextLocale]</span> variable expansion in TOC files, which will expand out to the client text locale (eg. "enUS").
* Added support for the <span class="apitype">[AllowLoadTextLocale ...]</span> conditional line directive in TOC files, which allows restricting files to only load under specific client text locales.
* The API documentation has been expanded with annotations for functions that have security restrictions in place.
* The {{api|t=a|CreateFromMixins}} and {{api|t=a|Mixin}} APIs are now implemented as native functions. Previously, [https://www.townlong-yak.com/framexml/11.1.7/Blizzard%20SharedXMLBase/Mixin.lua they were defined in Lua].
* {{api|t=w|Region:ClearAllPoints()}} now immediately invalidates the rect. Any measurement calculations relying on the previous rect should occur before calling ClearAllPoints.

==Breaking changes==
* The <code>StaticPopup_DisplayedFrames</code> and <code>STATICPOPUP_NUMDIALOGS</code> global variables have been removed.
** Addons wanting to iterate over shown static popup dialogs should instead use [https://github.com/Gethe/wow-ui-source/blob/e1cb04e86bcc9cda5af916300e163962d31c3a7d/Interface/AddOns/Blizzard_StaticPopup/StaticPopup.lua#L125 StaticPopup_ForEachShownDialog].
* Various child key references on StaticPopup dialogs have been renamed.
** Addons should prefer to use [https://github.com/Gethe/wow-ui-source/blob/e1cb04e86bcc9cda5af916300e163962d31c3a7d/Interface/AddOns/Blizzard_StaticPopup_Game/GameDialog.lua#L494-L528 the new accessor methods on StaticPopup frames] to access regions such as Buttons and EditBoxes.

